    bottomLine: "The curved trainer to compare a TrueForm Trainer against: longer surface, bigger review base, similar price.",
    description: "The AssaultRunner Pro is the machine most buyers compare with a TrueForm. Assault and independent reviews agree on a 17 by 62-inch slatted surface, a 350 lb maximum user weight and a 280 lb assembled weight, with a battery console that connects over Bluetooth and ANT+. It has no resistance setting, incline or fold. Its curve is deeper than TrueForm’s, which makes it eager to speed up when you lean in; that suits sprinting and feels busier at a steady jog. Assault’s frame term differs between its current page (7 years) and dealers and reviews (5 years), so get it in writing. US dealers listed it at $3,499 in early November 2026. See our full review for the detail.",
