    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">November 5, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.1k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read TrueForm's US store (trueformrunner.com), including the product
          data behind the TRUEFORM.RUNNER, TRUEFORM.TRAINER and TRUEFORM.ENDURO listings and every
          price option on them, its Runner-versus-Trainer comparison page, its warranty page and its
          Performance Adapter listing. We cross-checked the figures against Rogue Fitness's US
          listings for the Trainer and the Runner, Sorinex's Runner listing, and independent coverage
          from TreadmillReviews.com (Runner, updated March 2024), Garage Gym Lab (Trainer, December
          2023) and an October 2026 curved-treadmill comparison on ocdevel.com. We searched the US
          Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for TrueForm and True Form and found no
          recall. Figures on the product cards are those on which TrueForm or an official dealer and at
          least one independent source agree; where they disagree, we say so in the text and leave the
          figure off the card. The AssaultRunner Pro and SOLE C80 cards use specifications already
          cross-checked on this site in October 2026, with prices checked again on 5 November. We have
          not tested any TrueForm treadmill, and none of these figures are our own measurements. Prices
          and lead times are what the sellers showed on 5 November 2026 and change often, so confirm
          them for your exact configuration before you order. TrueForm sells direct and through
          dealers, not on Amazon, so its buttons below go to a tagged Amazon search that may show
          only similar curved manual treadmills. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases; it does not change
          which machines we list or what we say about them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
      <div class="not-prose bg-orange-50 border border-orange-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-3">Our Top Picks</h2>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0">
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
