            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a TrueForm Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A TrueForm is a large, expensive, specialised purchase that is hard to return. These are the ways buyers end up disappointed with one.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the Runner for home use because it is the famous one</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Most of what the Runner adds over the Trainer is build weight, US assembly, tread choice and facility branding. For one runner at home, the Trainer gives the same curve philosophy and a 400 lb rating for about half the money and ships in days rather than weeks. Decide which Runner-only feature you actually need before paying for it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting it to suit long walks</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A shallow curve with a heavy belt rewards a purposeful stride and makes a slow, relaxed walk hard work. Independent reviewers describe the TrueForm as a running and training tool rather than a desk-walking machine. If you mainly walk, a motorized treadmill or a deeper-curved trainer will be more comfortable.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every TrueForm has resistance</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Neither the Runner nor the Trainer has a resistance dial. Extra tension on the Runner comes from the separate Performance Adapter tether, and the Trainer cannot take it. If sled-style pushes and resisted sprints are your main use, a magnetic-brake trainer such as the SOLE C80 or the Bells of Steel Blitz is the better fit.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring freight and the floor</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Both machines weigh around 300 to 350 lb and arrive by freight. Buyers who have not measured the route to the room or checked whether delivery includes carrying it inside end up stuck with a crate on the drive. Plan the route, the floor and a heavy mat before ordering.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

